    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. one more thing though—sometimes when we run automated tests, we find these really weird, tiny glitches that don't seem to have a clear cause, like a button that intermittently disappears or a label that suddenly becomes unreadable for a split second. what's the best way to approach tracking down those kinds of irregular, hard-to-find bugs during an audit?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those intermittent glitches sound like classic \"flaky\" bugs, which are notoriously difficult to track down. You'll need to move beyond simple automated scans and embrace a more rigorous, manual, and observational approach. It's very helpful to use browser developer tools to monitor the DOM (Document Object Model) in real-time while reproducing the issue, looking for timing errors or race conditions. Furthermore, incorporating user testing with diverse assistive technology users is crucial, as these subtle timing issues often only manifest under specific, real-world usage patterns.",
      "source": "target",
