    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i've been trying the dev tools thing but it's like they're gone as soon as i look at them. it's super frustrating. are there any specific ways to document these \"ghost\" issues for the dev team so they don't just dismiss them as one-offs? i want to make sure they understand how much these little errors mess with the user flow.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When dealing with these elusive \"ghost\" issues, the documentation needs to be as detailed as a miniature, highly specific blueprint for a very rare event. Don't just say \"it disappeared\"; you need to capture the *context* of the disappearance, like a very specific sequence of actions, which is often the key to catching the bug. Try to record a video walkthrough of the exact sequence that triggers the glitch, overlaid with timestamps. This visual evidence, coupled with console logs captured *during* the event, is far more persuasive than a simple bug report.",
      "source": "target",
